2.
What
is
the
2024
COD-PS
update
for
Haiti?
The
2024
Common
Operational
Dataset
on
Population
Statistics
(COD-PS)
2
update
for
Haiti
is
the
best
available
set
of
subnational
population
projections,
disaggregated
by
sex,
5-year
age
groups
and
down
to
ADM-2
geographic
areas,
that
can
support
operational
humanitarian
response
actions.
The
2024
COD-PS
update
has
a
reference
date
of
September,
2024.
It
uses
the
2003
population
and
housing
census
data
as
a
baseline
population
and
projects
the
population
forward
to
a
reference
date
of
September
2024,
by
using
population
data
from
censuses,
surveys,
UNHCR
registration
data,
and
IOM’s
Displacement
Tracking
Matrix
to
account
for
population
change
across
departments
and
communes
of
Haiti
since
the
2003
census.
3.
What
are
some
of
the
key
insights
from
the
2024
COD-PS
update
in
Haiti?
This
2024
COD-PS
update
projects
the
population
of
Haiti
to
be
approximately
11.9
million
persons,
as
of
September
2024,
comprising
approximately
6.06
million
females
and
5.84
million
males
In
addition
to
the
mortality
and
fertility
effects
of
gang-related
violence,
natural
disasters,
and
fragility,
the
largest
component
of
population
change
in
recent
years
has
been
crisis-related
mobility
–
both
across
international
borders
and
within
the
administrative
boundaries
of
Haiti.
This
COD-PS
update
highlights
the
impact
of
this
demographic
change
on
the
subnational
population
size
and
age/sex
structure
of
Haiti,
as
shown
in
Figure
1.
As
discussed
in
technical
accompanying
documentation,
the
2024
COD-PS
update
draws
on
the
best
available
data
on
population
dynamics
in
Haiti,
integrates
these
data
using
well-established
demographic
modeling
and
estimation
techniques,
and
confirms
the
plausibility
and
reliability
of
the
resulting
estimates
via
cross-validation
with
other
available
data
and
estimates.
However,
the
calibration
and
cross-validation
of
the
2024
COD-PS
update
is
limited
by
notable
data
gaps,
data
quality
and
interoperability/alignment
issues
for
population
and
demographic
data
in
Haiti.
Despite
these
limitations
and
challenges,
the
2024
COD-PS
update
synthesizes
the
best
available
data
across
both
the
official
statistical
system
and
humanitarian
data
ecosystem
and
represents
the
best
available
population
baseline
estimates
for
humanitarian
decision-making
and
action.
2
The
Common
Operational
Dataset
on
Population
Statistics
(COD-PS)
is
a
set
of
up-to-date
(i.e.
reference
date
within
the
last
year)
subnational
population
projections,
disaggregated
by
sex
and
age
(standard
5-year
demographic
age
groups)
to
the
lowest
geographic
administrative
level
possible.
The
COD-PS
is
constructed
according
to
“best
available
humanitarian
data”
standards
and
designed
to
support
short-term
humanitarian
decision-making.
The
COD-PS
is
one
of
3
mandatory
common
operational
datasets,
alongside
common
operational
datasets
on
administrative
boundaries
and
humanitarian
caseloads,
that
are
required
in
all
operational
humanitarian
response
countries
by
the
United
Nations.
Ensuring
the
availability,
quality
and
usability
of
the
COD-PS
is
an
institutional
responsibility
of
the
United
Nations
Population
Fund
(UNFPA)
within
the
United
Nations
humanitarian
system.
