11.
There
are
notable
data
gaps
and
data
quality
challenges
associated
with
available
population
and
demographic
data
for
Haiti.
How
does
the
COD-PS
release
account
for
uncertainty
around
estimates
of
recent
demographic
change
in
Haiti?
Population
projections
such
as
those
used
in
the
2024
COD-PS
are
shaped
by
the
assumptions
and
input
data
used.
As
highlighted
throughout
the
preceding
section,
there
is
considerable
uncertainty
around
the
measurement
of
recent
demographic
change
in
Haiti,
especially
related
to
mobility,
but
also
related
to
mortality,
fertility,
and
the
adjustment
of
the
baseline
population
used.
Although
the
COD-PS
aims
to
use
the
most
plausible
assumptions,
in
close
alignment
with
best
available
data,
a
single
point
estimate
is
unlikely
to
fully
reflect
the
potential
for
variation
in
the
key
inputs
used.
In
order
to
support
humanitarian
end-users
seeking
to
understand
the
potential
range
of
uncertainty
associated
with
these
projections,
this
COD-PS
release
includes
an
additional,
experimental
dataset
that
provides
an
uncertainty
range
around
the
“median”
estimate,
which
is
used
in
the
COD-PS
projection.
This
dataset
should
be
considered
an
additional
source
of
information,
not
a
substitute
for
the
main
COD-PS
release,
which
remains
the
authoritative
reference
dataset
developed
for
the
HNRP
process.
Further
details
on
the
construction
of
this
uncertainty
range
are
available
in
the
technical
accompanying
note.
12.
What
are
the
ongoing
efforts
by
UNFPA
to
strengthen
future
COD-PS
updates
in
Haiti?
UNFPA
continues
to
support
efforts
to
strengthen
the
use
of
population
data
and
